 "description": "agentscan: Identify an x402 client by User-Agent: monitor, indexer, grader or HTTP library, with call rate. For any other User-Agent use parse_user_agent; for a whole access log use analyze_agent_traffic. Returns whether a User-Agent is a known x402 monitor, indexer, grader, SDK, AI fetcher, bot or HTTP library, what it does and its observed call rate at one seller (requests a day, per route, unpaid share); no `ua`: the full table. Input: optional `ua`; GET takes it as a query parameter. Reviewed table from one seller's logs and public docs; observed kinds are not confirmed by the operators. Unknown is `known` false (charged). The ua is not stored. Typically under 0.1 s. Price: USD 0.001. Free: 10 agent-index calls per IP per UTC day. Docs: https://tanod.dev/learn/x402-client-identify-api.html",
 "inputSchema": {
  "properties": {
   "ua": {
    "anyOf": [
     {
      "maxLength": 512,
      "type": "string"
     },
     {
      "type": "null"
     }
    ],
    "default": null,
    "description": "Optional: a User-Agent string to identify (at most 512 characters; not stored or echoed). Empty or absent: the whole table.",
    "title": "Ua"
   }
  },
